<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>🔴 Live: Chaotic scenes as organisers of French protests claim 800,000 have taken to streets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19a99da999b0219a45712802a5a160143e46940f92a4d2717737d9408ed4b832</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T17:18:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests" /></entry><entry><title>India: Police crack down on New Delhi protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcc63975bb3734fc0157445bca1d18f333f59d52c182b277541cb032ad01b358</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T16:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-india-police-crack-down-on-new-delhi-protests" /><summary type="html">Student activist Neha Bora, a prominent face of the protests, ‌who was detained on Friday as she tried to reach central Delhi with dozens of supporters, was released on Saturday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Amazon deforestation at 40-year low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab20c7c7c0a7c8b3ea82e909d8b733f14356369debf2bc30237ece7f5dddea69</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T16:07:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-brazil-amazon-deforestation-at-40-year-low" /><summary type="html">In Brazil, deforestation in the Amazon has reached its lowest level in 40 years. President Lula is bolstering his environmental record just over a week before the second round of the presidential election, in which he faces Flávio Bolsonaro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war: "Mothers of Kherson" opera opens in Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abeeaf69b9ec540a23f999b6c19c8960048133821dca9c671eb96f6cd3a0d81f</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:57:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-ukraine-war-mothers-of-kherson-opera-opens-in-poland" /><summary type="html">"Mothers of Kherson" has opened at Poland's National Opera. The performance was co-produced with New York's Metropolitan Opera and created in close association with Save Ukraine, a group helping to bring back Ukrainian children who remain in Russia. More than four years after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, the opera aims to "reawaken" global interest in the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Protests in France: "Two fires broke out in Place de la République"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc0bbefed5933bf75ef837990bcbbfbd87e46f0f16d7e62323949ab997a0eeda</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:53:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-two-fires-broke-out-in-place-de-la-r%C3%A9publique" /><summary type="html">Police and protesters clashed in Paris and other French cities on Saturday, with smoke from fires and tear gas filling the air at demonstrations nationwide against high prices, ahead of elections to replace President Emmanuel Macron. "Two fires broke out in Place de la République," reports France 24's Antonia Kerrigan from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Protester’s hand blown off by police grenade as unions say half a million march across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adf42f149a03f56a004c13d985283aec4ef436b45766c8421bc637d7bf2190ca</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:25:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests" /></entry><entry><title>US: Four killed in Oregon school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a901bd5d40b848c2f8e836364498e73154888de435e00f0dbb0adfebc09a836</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:16:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-us-four-killed-in-oregon-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The teenage gunman who shot dead three children and a teacher in an Oregon school was a former special needs student there, officials said Friday, as they praised the heroism of people who helped to shorten the rampage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Protests in France: "Living conditions are too harsh"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af2f08b62e0d6bfc21adb471b419a33dc8d733696df9c187d32621016ea652f6</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:10:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-living-conditions-are-too-harsh" /><summary type="html">Saturday’s mobilisation in France follows calls on social media to revive the Yellow Vests movement, which emerged in 2018 against social injustice. Student groups protesting since mid-September have urged supporters to join. We discuss this with our journalist on the ground, Antonia Kerrigan, and our guest, Paul Smith, head of Modern Languages at the University of Nottingham.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: What's different about today's protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eafeddf941a16e2b91b5a1fee8b830244cf8092a71bffc71fe2cd5a9362cd4fa</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:07:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-france-what-s-different-about-today-s-protests" /><summary type="html">In France, protests are under way across the country this Saturday. Demonstrators are protesting against the high cost of living, as well as poor working and studying conditions. We discuss this with France 24's Jamie Smith-Maillet.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Israeli settlers beat French mayor, attack European diplomatic cars in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af9ceea06b6fff58efcf7d1b3dd6427c004a8aaa03896f71039b8de98f667101</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:58:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261017-israeli-settlers-attack-european-delegation-convoy-in-west-bank-beat-french-mayor" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli settlers attack European delegation convoy in West Bank, beat French mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:601e6ac728ce0326fa5d34a81f77f1099ac9dc52405d985f5a2e0d45fdbf4182</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:58:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261017-israeli-settlers-attack-european-delegation-convoy-in-west-bank-beat-french-mayor" /><summary type="html">Israeli settlers have attacked a convoy carrying a European delegation in the occupied West Bank and beat up a French mayor, witnesses said Saturday.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>France: "We've seen extremely high tensions between protesters and law enforcement"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:857dcffc0fffa00e71cd40accef532d1375ad171be1b5f7ae0e1ee0296ddeda7</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:46:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-france-we-ve-seen-extremely-high-tensions-between-protesters-and-law-enforcement" /><summary type="html">Protesters across France called for street demonstrations on Saturday against rising living costs. France 24's Antonia Kerrigan reports from Paris.

"The march from here to Place de Clichy isn't set to start for another hour. However, we've seen it kicking off extremely early doors. It seems that what's happened is that police attempted to block the protesters from reaching Place de la République, and we saw the use of tear gas. We've seen people running with their masks on. We also saw the use of stun grenades."</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Students, unions and Yellow Vests unite against austerity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5285362c55374bfa5569e6d6a0a68b2ed3392a9d20f0f5312c48d6b87c0182a1</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:45:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-france-students-unions-and-yellow-vests-unite-against-austerity" /><summary type="html">190 000 people could demonstrate this Saturday in France. They called for street demonstrations Saturday against rising living costs, joining high school students' grievances over education conditions after more than three weeks of school blockades.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Paramount’s creation of Skydance test France’s cultural exception?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1443023de2a0156d3b9f6aad84da631a4bee4df660817a3bc319a18f1e753907</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-will-paramount-creation-of-skydance-test-france-cultural-exception" /><summary type="html">Skydance’s $110 billion creation tests whether France’s cultural exception can still compel a leveraged global media giant to fund, protect and prioritise French creativity, or merely treat it as a compliance cost.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Looting, blazes and clashes in France amid nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e980b6194cf2e21d1bc22f99970b2a6c59923579b2680364c80ffc7a127b22e</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T12:31:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261017-french-protesters-clash-with-police-during-nationwide-demonstrations" /><summary type="html">Police and protesters clashed violently in Paris and other French cities Saturday on the sidelines of nationwide marches against soaring inflation, with one demonstrator's hand blown off, multiple blazes set and looters breaking into dozens of stores to strip them bare.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Tens of thousands join protests across France, clashes reported in several cities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bbb43225fb0d7369899671ec96a902bf9b4cdcb24bff89431ce42c93f6ddea1</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T12:30:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests" /></entry><entry><title>France faces day of cost-of-living protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:015205af5b267fc00c59c5619891caf50530eb5d626c98f7cb83b73ebf5e0aef</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:47:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-france-faces-day-of-cost-of-living-protests" /><summary type="html">French authorities detained dozens on Saturday at the start of nationwide protests against the cost of living, in what is likely to be a key indicator of the social climate heading toward elections to replace President Emmanuel Macron. France 24's Antonia Kerrigan tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cameroonian journalist shot in Bamenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7388156118b5ee2f9828aeaf7092be2690a60452fc4bc3d118bf9056e5597269</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:16:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-cameroonian-journalist-shot-in-bamenda" /><summary type="html">Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in the north-western city of Bamenda. A young woman was also killed as the attackers opened fire on mourners attending a wake. The shooting has renewed concerns about the dangers facing journalists in Cameroon's English-speaking regions, after years of conflict between government forces and separatist groups.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uganda launches Ebola vaccine trial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ffe2b61be7046a263a2cdb28aa49613489a2af5740bf61dbc297a6cd8fb76d8</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:00:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-uganda-launches-ebola-vaccine-trial" /><summary type="html">The town of Masaka in southern Uganda is currently conducting a Phase 1 trial of a vaccine candidate against the Bundibugyo strain of the Ebola virus, which is circulating in the region. There is currently no approved treatment or vaccine for this strain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports third Ebola case, contact tracing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48e778593bb40e115dd87644c3a9184b4a595144c07056e324962d12e83c111e</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:56:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-kenya-reports-third-ebola-case-contact-tracing-continues" /><summary type="html">Kenya has confirmed a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from the Democratic Republic of the Congo. The health ministry said the 65-year-old woman tested positive while in quarantine, where she has been since 5 October. The second patient, a 39-year-old man from the same family, is in a stable condition. Health officials say there is no evidence of community transmission, as both individuals were under quarantine. However, three contacts have yet to be traced. Our correspondent Bastien Renouil tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia hails Trump waiving sanctions as 'historic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be9db540322e486e23eeaf8472606421bf514d2ea59bacc1aa861eb97d66a23a</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:41:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-russia-hails-trump-waiving-sanctions-as-historic" /><summary type="html">Russia on Saturday hailed US President Donald Trump's move to waive new sanctions on it as "historic", as Ukraine worries he is taking Moscow's side in Europe's worst conflict since World War II.</summary></entry><entry><title>Coastal homes burn as hot winds fuel California fires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:779ddb48e1e58cc2a1a05c96b9c7c0963e7841a9bf39cc85b65a4af83e5ff4e7</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:37:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-coastal-homes-burn-as-hot-winds-fuel-california-fires" /><summary type="html">A fast-moving fire fueled by high winds burned at least six homes in Southern California on Friday, engulfing expensive coastal properties and prompting thousands to evacuate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump's new press secretary out after less than week</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a43a94441bdc884ef97a841877ddf62d2413f60d546c1bd3dfa5d644a7a407a1</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:36:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-trump-s-new-press-secretary-out-after-less-than-week" /><summary type="html">White House Press Secretary Katie Zacharia was pushed out Friday after less than a week in the high-profile job following a series of blunders that added to distractions for her embattled boss, President Donald Trump.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo returns to Vatican four days after lung cancer surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c95559dcaac6586c05d6f97ce4868f440e8e61c650f7afd8c9924969995fb508</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:35:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261017-pope-leo-returns-to-vatican-four-days-after-lung-cancer-surgery" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV was released from the hospital on Saturday after lung cancer surgery. Doctors removed part of the 71-year-old's right lung last week to extract a cancerous tumour.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
